# What does NOT go into the VSIX.
#
# The shipped artifact is `dist/` plus `package.json`, `README.md`, `LICENSE`
# and `SECURITY.md`. Everything else here is source, fixtures or tooling.
#
# `SECURITY.md` ships deliberately. Zero egress and the read-only posture are
# this extension's trust anchor, so the document asserting them belongs inside
# the artifact a user actually installs, not only in a repository they may
# never visit. It was checked for absolute paths before that decision: it
# contains none, which is the property that keeps `fixtures/**` out below.
#
# Two entries are load-bearing rather than tidy:
#
#   fixtures/**   The capture is CONTENT-FREE but not anonymous: it keeps
#                 `cwd`, `transcript_path`, `session_id` and `agent_id`
#                 verbatim because a fixture without them cannot pin the
#                 main-thread rule. Shipping it inside a VSIX would publish
#                 one developer's absolute paths. It is excluded here as well
#                 as by `!` ordering so no future glob can readmit it.
#   **/*.map      Source maps embed absolute source paths from the build
#                 machine. `npm run build -- --production` emits none; this is
#                 the belt to that braces, so a non-production build packaged
#                 by accident still ships no paths.

.vscode/**
.vscode-test/**
.claude/**
.github/**
.git/**
.gitattributes
.gitignore
.vscodeignore

src/**
webview/**
test/**
spike/**
fixtures/**
node_modules/**

**/*.ts
**/*.svelte
**/*.map
**/*.test.*
**/tsconfig*.json
**/*.tsbuildinfo

esbuild.config.mjs
eslint.config.js
vitest.config.ts
package-lock.json

PLAN.md
CLAUDE.md
HANDOVER.md
agent-deck-spec.md

# Historical v1 documents. `docs/README.md` is the only doc a user wants, and
# it is deliberately NOT excluded — there is no root README yet (Phase 5 owns
# it), so this is what the VSIX ships.
docs/PLAN-v1.md
docs/agent-deck-spec-v1.md

# Dev tooling and design artifacts. None of it is part of the product, and
# `vsce ls` was shipping all three before this: the two recorder/capture
# scripts, the frozen canvas design docs (a 38 KB mockup), and the UI-state
# evidence. Checked for leaked absolute paths first - there are none, so this
# is bloat rather than a privacy defect - but a VSIX should carry the product,
# not the workshop.
scripts/**
docs/ui/**
docs/evidence/**

# The replay theater is DEV-ONLY and must never reach a user. It is unreachable
# from `webview/main.ts` (asserted on esbuild's import graph), and `webview/**`
# below already keeps its source out -- but `node esbuild.config.mjs --theater`
# emits into `dist/`, which this file ships wholesale. `--theater` is opt-in and
# is not part of `npm run build`, so the default path was already safe; this
# line closes the case where someone builds it before packaging. That is the
# "manifest and build disagree" class CLAUDE.md records, and it has bitten this
# repo before.
dist/theater/**

# The VSIX itself. `--out dist/agent-deck.vsix` writes into a directory this
# file otherwise ships wholesale, so without this line the second `npm run
# package` embeds the first one's artifact.
dist/*.vsix
